WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:04.980
Yeah…this is going to go down as one of
the best action movies of all time.

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:09.990
And honestly, this is probably the best action
franchise of all time given how consistently

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:13.210
magnificent each one of the John Wick movies
have been.

00:00:13.210 --> 00:00:16.990
But somehow, this 4th installment blows the
rest out of the water.

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:21.390
You know how in the last movie where in the
continental hotel, John Wick and the staff

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:25.390
have to fight an army of high table soldiers
with bulletproof armor; which essentially

00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:28.010
acts as the major climax of that film?

00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:32.800
Well in John Wick 4, that’s the level the
action starts at and it keeps getting raised

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:36.680
from there like someone doing the salmon ladder
jump in Ninja Warrior.

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:41.120
Each consecutive scene elevates the action
and either gives some cool variation in either

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:45.560
the physical aspect or something visually
spectacular is happening on screen to make

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:50.390
up for the fact that John Wick isn’t doing
constant 360 noscopes while running around

00:00:50.390 --> 00:00:51.629
in Paris.

00:00:51.629 --> 00:00:54.460
Because that’s essentially the last 30 minutes
of the movie.

00:00:54.460 --> 00:00:59.730
It's a constant marathon of outstanding action
that offers unique elements in each set piece.

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:04.030
It kind of reminds me of Jackie Chan films
where every action scene uses the environment

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:05.350
in some creative way.

00:01:05.350 --> 00:01:09.840
And in John Wick 4, almost every scene has
a fun angle it plays with.

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:14.140
Whether it being John fighting people in the
middle of busy traffic, fighting on a massive

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:18.630
staircase where people are rolling down endless
flights of stars, or picking up a gun that

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:20.530
shoots flammable rounds.

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:24.970
John Wick doesn’t necessarily interact with
the environment as much as Jackie Chan does,

00:01:24.970 --> 00:01:29.310
but the setting in which the action takes
place keeps everything fresh and exciting.

00:01:29.310 --> 00:01:32.470
Making it to where the choreographers are
always having a field day in how John Wick

00:01:32.470 --> 00:01:34.140
dispatches his foes.

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:38.390
Another great thing is that the enemies here
mostly have bulletproof suits, so it makes

00:01:38.390 --> 00:01:40.820
them much harder to overcome for John.

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:45.350
In the earlier movies, it became a bit annoying
how easy it was for John to clear rooms full

00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:46.350
of people.

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:50.619
Now that isn’t an issue because each foe
he faces feels like a major obstacle.

00:01:50.619 --> 00:01:55.340
So the main solution to killing these enemies
is getting creative with up-close combat.

00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:59.100
Even though John Wick is supposed to be the
deadliest assassin, he’s still being pushed

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:00.369
to his limits here.

00:02:00.369 --> 00:02:04.770
Meaning that the conflict he has to overcome
is that much better than prior movies.

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:09.780
They also made it to where John is not able
to execute constant headshots, so it’s nice

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:13.129
that he’s a bit more realistic in terms
of what he can achieve.

00:02:13.129 --> 00:02:18.190
In the first couple of movies, him running
into a room instantly killing everyone started

00:02:18.190 --> 00:02:22.879
to become stale to a degree because it lacked
that hard conflict for John.

00:02:22.879 --> 00:02:27.670
So every scene in John Wick 4 isn’t hindered
by that fact and tests him.

00:02:27.670 --> 00:02:31.879
And even though some enemies don’t have
bulletproof armor, they’ll still throw dozens

00:02:31.879 --> 00:02:36.620
of people at John at a time or introduce some
other elements to spice up the scene.

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:40.310
Like an example being people trying to run
over John with cars.

00:02:40.310 --> 00:02:44.129
Action of this caliber is extremely rare and
this is the utter peak of what the genre has

00:02:44.129 --> 00:02:45.819
to offer in my opinion.

00:02:45.819 --> 00:02:48.860
This is a gold standard for high-budget action.

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:53.500
Actually, on the topic of budget, it’s crazy
to me that John Wick 4 has a budget of 100

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:59.210
million dollars and other action movies are
significantly more expensive and are worse.

00:02:59.210 --> 00:03:04.620
As an example, a recent bad action movie I
saw was The Gray Man rocking a budget of 200

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:06.080
million dollars.

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:10.769
So the fact that John Wick 4 has half the
budget and is infinitely better is funny to

00:03:10.769 --> 00:03:11.769
me.

00:03:11.769 --> 00:03:16.260
Kind of goes to show that practical and realistic
action will always trump VFX mayhem.

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:20.519
If this film doesn’t satisfy you, then I
don’t know what action movie will.

00:03:20.519 --> 00:03:25.349
Because even the first act of the movie basically
has one massive uninterrupted action scene

00:03:25.349 --> 00:03:28.050
that felt like it lasted for over 30 minutes.

00:03:28.050 --> 00:03:32.270
It just floors you right out of the gate and
if you think it can’t get better, it somehow

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:33.590
does.

00:03:33.590 --> 00:03:38.880
One complaint that I assume may bug some people
is that the movie is 3 hours long and personally,

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:41.110
I think it earns that runtime.

00:03:41.110 --> 00:03:44.299
Action takes up the bulk of the screen time
and it makes the movie feel like it’s 2

00:03:44.299 --> 00:03:45.299
hours long.

00:03:45.299 --> 00:03:50.520
Chad Stahelski said that the original cut
was almost 4 hours and I’d honestly love

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:52.930
to see that as a director’s cut or something.

00:03:52.930 --> 00:03:58.270
John Wick 4 has quite a bit of scenes dedicated
to story and character development and I think

00:03:58.270 --> 00:04:02.570
they did a great job with them in comparison
to the last couple of John Wick movies.

00:04:02.570 --> 00:04:06.780
Because for the last 2, they set up some silly
notions within the world like practically

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:11.180
everyone on the streets being assassins and
the weird desert scene where John has to find

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:12.180
the Elder.

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:16.530
In John Wick 4, everything feels more straightforward
and there’s never a moment in which I’m

00:04:16.530 --> 00:04:19.600
scratching my head because of some weird writing
decisions.

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:23.781
The movie doesn’t retcon anything so these
past writing choices are still present, but

00:04:23.781 --> 00:04:28.440
everything that’s introduced going forward
is good and plausible for the world.

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:32.350
Like a lot of new high-table information is
established in this movie and I just found

00:04:32.350 --> 00:04:34.070
all that really fascinating.

00:04:34.070 --> 00:04:38.600
The characters were all interesting and were
very complex with varying motivations.

00:04:38.600 --> 00:04:42.690
They had cool dynamics and seeing them clash
on screen were some of the best fights so

00:04:42.690 --> 00:04:43.690
far.

00:04:43.690 --> 00:04:47.630
Like Donnie Yen’s character is John’s
friend but is essentially forced into a position

00:04:47.630 --> 00:04:50.229
where he has to hunt him down for the high
table.

00:04:50.229 --> 00:04:54.910
But the entire time while doing so, they have
this layer of respect for each other.

00:04:54.910 --> 00:04:58.610
Donnie Yen is also blind in the movie and
that offers a cool perspective in terms of

00:04:58.610 --> 00:04:59.610
action.

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:04.070
It’s kind of crazy how he’s able to dispatch
of people with this hindrance and he is basically

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:06.770
Daredevil but as Donnie Yen.

00:05:06.770 --> 00:05:11.041
Going back to the fact that John Wick is constantly
being tested, seeing Donnie Yen’s character

00:05:11.041 --> 00:05:14.360
overcome his conflict in fights is also great.

00:05:14.360 --> 00:05:18.970
A blind Donnie Yen rolling people would be
the price of admission alone for me, let alone

00:05:18.970 --> 00:05:21.400
everything else the movie offers.

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:25.160
Then the other new assassin character has
some cool weapons he uses throughout the movie

00:05:25.160 --> 00:05:28.350
while also having a loyal dog that helps him
in combat.

00:05:28.350 --> 00:05:32.630
At each point in the story he has a fun dynamic
with one of the characters and his relationship

00:05:32.630 --> 00:05:34.910
with Bill Skarsgard was really funny.

00:05:34.910 --> 00:05:39.300
So in comparison to some of the other assassins
in the earlier films, this roster is more

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:41.590
varied and fun all around.

00:05:41.590 --> 00:05:45.080
Along with them having a more consistent presence
within the plot.

00:05:45.080 --> 00:05:49.280
So it makes them more relevant and have character
arcs throughout the story.

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:53.199
Instead of being an assassin who shows up
to fight John and that being it.

00:05:53.199 --> 00:05:57.890
The effort being put forward by the writers
for this movie feels like an upgrade overall.

00:05:57.890 --> 00:06:03.000
The stakes and tension feel extremely palpable
in every scene and the scenarios they concoct

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:04.280
are genius to me.

00:06:04.280 --> 00:06:08.050
An example of that is making it to where John
has to fight through Paris under a strict

00:06:08.050 --> 00:06:09.340
time constraint.

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:14.340
It just made the ending feel like an incredible
rush and it really gets your adrenaline pumping.

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:17.360
Even the dialogue scenes are injected with
suspense.

00:06:17.360 --> 00:06:21.139
Like there’s a lot of posturing between
the characters and you never really know how

00:06:21.139 --> 00:06:24.120
they’ll interact given their complex histories.

00:06:24.120 --> 00:06:28.330
It makes them that much more engaging to watch
because there is so much subtext to be mined

00:06:28.330 --> 00:06:29.770
from each character.

00:06:29.770 --> 00:06:33.610
The writers don’t flat-out tell you their
backstories and it’s fun to infer from the

00:06:33.610 --> 00:06:37.310
subtle information we are given as to what
happened in the past.

00:06:37.310 --> 00:06:42.090
So the writers are able to make even the dialogue
scenes good and this paired with a solid pace

00:06:42.090 --> 00:06:44.850
makes the movie feel like a great 3 hours.

00:06:44.850 --> 00:06:49.330
And from this better writing, I think they
have the best villain in Bill Skarsgard.

00:06:49.330 --> 00:06:53.830
His accent was a little annoying to me, but
he was very menacing despite not particularly

00:06:53.830 --> 00:06:55.660
being physically powerful.

00:06:55.660 --> 00:07:00.190
Bill has a way of getting under your skin
with his unsettling vibes and as one of the

00:07:00.190 --> 00:07:03.449
most powerful men in the world, he slays it.

00:07:03.449 --> 00:07:07.940
That and he’s also dressed in some insane
drip, so visually he’s a tour de force.

00:07:07.940 --> 00:07:12.740
The overall cast is just stacked and I remember
when they were announcing them one by one

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:15.270
it was like unwrapping Christmas presents.

00:07:15.270 --> 00:07:20.240
This is literally a once-in-a-lifetime ensemble
cast and seeing these people on screen together

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:22.289
was a constant delight.

00:07:22.289 --> 00:07:26.960
Scott Adkins in particular, who hasn’t had
many popular roles really stole his scenes

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:28.919
and I was kind of surprised by that.

00:07:28.919 --> 00:07:31.950
Another aspect about the movie I loved was
the music.

00:07:31.950 --> 00:07:36.150
It’s constantly bumping and the final act
has this person on a radio that broadcasts

00:07:36.150 --> 00:07:40.919
out to assassins and she keeps playing some
fun songs that carry over into the action

00:07:40.919 --> 00:07:41.919
scenes.

00:07:41.919 --> 00:07:46.009
It really energizes the last act and even
other scenes like the big club scene has loud

00:07:46.009 --> 00:07:50.590
booming music that puts you into a loving
trance for the spectacle on screen.

00:07:50.590 --> 00:07:55.160
Really every aspect of this movie is brilliant
and I will be kind of disappointed if the

00:07:55.160 --> 00:07:58.100
cinematographer doesn’t get any award recognition.

00:07:58.100 --> 00:08:00.220
Because this movie is gorgeous.

00:08:00.220 --> 00:08:04.150
The trailers as you can see here have some
incredible shots, but the entire movie carries

00:08:04.150 --> 00:08:06.669
on with these awe-inspiring visuals.

00:08:06.669 --> 00:08:10.889
The colors in every frame pop and are contrasted
so well.

00:08:10.889 --> 00:08:15.620
Like just a random example outside of the
action is John standing around in Japan silhouetted

00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:17.509
by some cool backdrops.

00:08:17.509 --> 00:08:21.610
The director and cinematographer picked some
great locations to film and every set piece

00:08:21.610 --> 00:08:23.389
is visual eye candy.

00:08:23.389 --> 00:08:25.370
Just like the last movies honestly.

00:08:25.370 --> 00:08:28.840
John Wick 4 also has one of my favorite oners
of all time.

00:08:28.840 --> 00:08:32.969
Like when the oner started I immediately leaned
forward in my seat and started uncontrollably

00:08:32.969 --> 00:08:35.360
smiling from how amazing it was.

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:41.290
John Wick running around eviscerating people
with flammable rounds is truly just peak cinema.

00:08:41.290 --> 00:08:45.220
The people in my theater were losing their
shit in almost every scene and you should

00:08:45.220 --> 00:08:48.080
really see this with your friends if they
appreciate action.

00:08:48.080 --> 00:08:52.410
I haven’t had this much fun in an action
movie since probably Mad Max: Fury Road.

00:08:52.410 --> 00:08:56.470
I’d be surprised if John Wick 4 is able
to receive the same respect as that movie

00:08:56.470 --> 00:09:00.910
because Fury Road got nominated for Best Picture,
but hey, we’ll see.

00:09:00.910 --> 00:09:04.980
It’s only like this will probably be the
best action movie you’ll see in the next

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:06.000
5 years or so.

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:10.430
I’m also going to go see John Wick 4 again
which is rare for me, especially considering

00:09:10.430 --> 00:09:11.950
it’s a three-hour movie.

00:09:11.950 --> 00:09:15.880
And I’m really excited to see how the Ana
De Armas’ movie Ballerina will be.

00:09:15.880 --> 00:09:19.680
Thank you for watching and let me know in
the comments what you thought about John Wick

00:09:19.680 --> 00:09:19.820
4.

